-- title:
--   A partition word has one entry per block
-- statement:
--   Let $h,J\in\mathbb N$, and let $t$ be a retained-choice tuple with one choice for each of the $J$ blocks. Its partition word lists, in block order, the left subset of the edge selected by each choice. Then
--
--   $$
--   |\operatorname{partitionWord}(t)|=J.
--   $$
--
--   This length identity aligns the finite choice tuple with the list of prefix decisions consumed by the reporting traversal.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/RawReporting.lean#L71-L72

